  "caveats": [
    "The initial 32-test run and unchanged original TCP replay passed before expanding the negatives and local-owner fence tests.",
    "The wider pre-fence run has one failure: the seven-kind dispatch fixture compared its original seven records against the expanded nine-kind export inventory. Both original-seven-kind fixtures now enumerate exactly the records they exercise; new checkpoint kinds have separate actual-storage/network qualification. The failed intermediate run was explicitly stopped after recording that failure and the two completed checkpoint-storage suites; its incomplete remainder is not reported green.",
    "The first fence regression invocation did not compile because the test caught an exception that observeCurrent does not throw. Its corrected two-test run reproduces both missing local-owner checks; both pass on the final source.",
    "A first 133-test qualification had one error: the unused-inventory adversarial fixture opened a metadata-only current generation without record-export ownership. It now opens the generation owner, first proves a valid ACK can be exported and checks both exact refusals. Its focused test passes; restoring the unsafe inventory-only export reproduces one expected assertion failure.",
    "The final build uses a fresh isolated directory and rechecks every Java/POM/resource input against the exact workspace. It includes all 16 checkpoint tests and associated activation, transfer, selection and API regressions.",
    "TCP scenarios use real public offline bootstrap and actual BARRIER/DATA publication before current-view ancestry retrieval. Fault delivery and copied-owner negatives are deterministic component tests; the unused-inventory negative uses a separate model/storage fixture.",
    "The higher capsule must already be verified. Full historical membership ACCEPT/PROOF provenance, unavailable original owners, automatic missing-ancestry discovery and cross-view adoption remain open.",
    "Autonomous election, repeated-round source maintenance, scratch crash recovery, learner/joint completion, generalized voting/publication and complete distributed S/N qualification remain required for Phase 3 closure."
  ],
